---
/**
 * FST 101 course section page for Dr. Leith's Fall 2026 sections T07 and T08.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY NOT A SYLLABUS. FST 101 is a department-owned course: the
 * syllabus, the graded structure, and the week-by-week schedule are set by the
 * course coordinator and distributed through Blackboard. Reproducing a
 * coordinator-owned document here would create a second copy that drifts, and
 * students would have no way to tell which one governs.
 *
 * What this page carries is the part that is genuinely section-specific and
 * genuinely stable: which room each section meets in, the eight dates it meets
 * on, how to reach me, and where campus help lives. That is the information
 * students most often cannot find, and none of it is mine to get wrong.
 */
import SyllabusLayout from '../../layouts/SyllabusLayout.astro';
import GettingHelp from '../../components/syllabus/GettingHelp.astro';

const BOOKINGS =
  'https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/b5d8aa74215e488fbf4d85ab72761ecf@siue.edu?anonymous&ismsaljsauthenabled&ep=plink';

const t07 = ['Aug 25', 'Sep 1', 'Sep 8', 'Sep 15', 'Sep 22', 'Sep 29', 'Oct 6', 'Oct 13'];
const t08 = ['Aug 27', 'Sep 3', 'Sep 10', 'Sep 17', 'Sep 24', 'Oct 1', 'Oct 8', 'Oct 15'];
---
<SyllabusLayout
  title="FST 101 Sections T07 and T08"
  description="FST 101 First Semester Transition, Fall 2026 sections T07 and T08 with Dr. Alex Leith at SIUE. Meeting times, rooms, dates, and where to get help."
  updated="August 17, 2026"
>
  <div class="syl-hero">
    <span class="syl-course">FST 101 &middot; Fall 2026 &middot; Sections T07 + T08</span>
    <h1 data-no-split>First Semester Transition</h1>
    <div class="syl-tagline">
      Succeeding and engaging at SIUE. Eight weeks, one 75-minute meeting a
      week, and a set of habits that make the next four years easier than the
      first eight weeks were.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="syl-actions syl-noprint">
    <button type="button" class="syl-btn" id="syl-print">Print this page</button>
    <a class="syl-btn" href="https://bb.siue.edu/">Blackboard</a>
    <a class="syl-btn" href="/students/">Student toolkit</a>
  </div>

  <ul class="syl-facts">
    <li>
      <span class="syl-fact-label">Section T07</span>
      <span class="syl-fact-value"><strong>Tuesdays, 2:00 to 3:15 PM</strong></span>
      <span class="syl-fact-note">Peck Hall 0406</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="syl-fact-label">Section T08</span>
      <span class="syl-fact-value"><strong>Thursdays, 2:00 to 3:15 PM</strong></span>
      <span class="syl-fact-note">Peck Hall 0408</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="syl-fact-label">Term</span>
      <span class="syl-fact-value"><strong>Aug 24 to Oct 16, 2026</strong></span>
      <span class="syl-fact-note">Eight weeks. This course ends at midterm, not at the end of the semester.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="syl-fact-label">Instructor</span>
      <span class="syl-fact-value"><strong>Alex P. Leith, PhD</strong></span>
      <span class="syl-fact-note">Alex, AP, or Dr. Leith. He / they.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="syl-fact-label">Office hours</span>
      <span class="syl-fact-value"><strong>Tu / Th, 12:30 to 1:45 and 3:30 to 5:00 PM</strong></span>
      <span class="syl-fact-note">1017 Dunham Hall, drop in. Both windows sit either side of our 2:00 class, so you can come straight before or straight after.</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="syl-fact-label">Email</span>
      <span class="syl-fact-value"><a href="mailto:aleith@siue.edu">aleith@siue.edu</a></span>
      <span class="syl-fact-note">Reply within 24 hours on weekdays</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <section class="syl-first-week">
    <h2>Start here</h2>
    <p>Four things, in the first week. None of them take long.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Check which section you are in.</strong> T07 meets Tuesdays in
        Peck Hall 0406. T08 meets Thursdays in Peck Hall 0408. Different
        sections, different rooms, and going to the wrong one is the most common
        first-week mistake.</li>
      <li><strong>Open the Blackboard course.</strong> The syllabus, the graded
        assignments, and the week-by-week schedule live there. That is the
        official version of all three.</li>
      <li><strong>Get the textbook.</strong> It is free. See below.</li>
      <li><strong>Email me if anything about week one is unclear.</strong> Asking
        early is not a bother; it is the whole point of a first-semester
        course.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <div class="syl-prose">

  <h2 id="what-this-page-is">What this page is</h2>

  <p>FST 101 is taught across many sections by many instructors, and the course
  is coordinated at the department level. <strong>The syllabus in your
  Blackboard course is the official one</strong>: it sets the assignments, the
  points, and the week-by-week schedule, and it governs if anything here and
  anything there ever disagree.</p>

  <p>This page carries the part that is specific to my two sections and that
  students most often cannot find: where we meet, when, how to reach me, and
  which campus office handles what.</p>

  <h2 id="meeting-dates">When we meet</h2>

  <p>Each section meets <strong>once a week for eight weeks</strong>. That is
  eight meetings total, so a single absence is an eighth of the course. If you
  have to miss one, tell me beforehand and we will sort out what you need.</p>

  <div class="syl-table-scroll">
    <table class="schedule-table">
      <caption>Meeting dates by section, Fall 2026</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Meeting</th>
          <th scope="col">T07 &middot; Tuesdays &middot; Peck Hall 0406</th>
          <th scope="col">T08 &middot; Thursdays &middot; Peck Hall 0408</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {t07.map((d, i) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{i + 1}</th>
            <td>{d}</td>
            <td>{t08[i]}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>Labor Day (Monday, September 7) does not fall on either meeting day, so no
  meeting is lost to it.</p>

  <h2 id="textbook">Textbook</h2>

  <p>The required textbook is <strong>OpenStax <em>College Success
  Concise</em></strong>, and it is <strong>free</strong>. OpenStax is an
  openly-licensed publisher; you can read it online, download the PDF, or buy a
  printed copy at cost if you prefer paper. Do not pay a third-party site for
  it. The link is in the Blackboard course, and the book is at
  <a href="https://openstax.org/">openstax.org</a>.</p>

  <p>Some weeks also draw on <em>Connections Are Everything</em>, which is
  likewise free to read online. Anything else you need is posted in
  Blackboard.</p>

  <h2 id="how-to-reach-me">How to reach me</h2>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Right before or right after class.</strong> My office hours are
      Tuesday and Thursday, 12:30 to 1:45 PM and 3:30 to 5:00 PM, in 1017 Dunham
      Hall. The first window ends fifteen minutes before your section starts and
      the second begins fifteen minutes after it ends. Walk over. No appointment
      needed.</li>
    <li><strong>Email</strong>
      (<a href="mailto:aleith@siue.edu">aleith@siue.edu</a>) for anything
      formal, confidential, or not urgent. I answer within 24 hours on
      weekdays.</li>
    <li><strong>By appointment, remotely</strong>, through
      <a href={BOOKINGS}>Microsoft Bookings</a>, which shows you only my open
      times.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Clearly stated needs save us both time. Tell me what you tried, what is not
  working, and what kind of help you are hoping for.</p>

  <h2 id="toolkit">The student toolkit</h2>

  <p>The AURA Lab keeps an open-source
  <a href="/students/">student toolkit</a>: a set of free tools for writing,
  citing, reading, note-taking, and keeping track of your work, with setup
  instructions. It is not a course requirement and nothing on it is graded. It
  exists because the software students are told to buy is usually replaceable by
  something free that does the job as well, and the first semester is the right
  time to find that out.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/students/">toolkit's front page</a> is laid out against the
  same eight weeks as your Blackboard course and in the same order, so the setup
  listed for a given week is the one that helps with what we are doing that
  week. You can also ignore the weeks entirely: go to the
  <a href="/students/toolkit/">toolkit index</a> and pick the one thing you are
  currently doing the hard way.</p>

  <GettingHelp />

  </div>
</SyllabusLayout>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    function wire() {
      var b = document.getElementById('syl-print');
      if (b && !b.dataset.wired) {
        b.dataset.wired = '1';
        b.addEventListener('click', function () { window.print(); });
      }
    }
    wire();
    document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', wire);
  })();
</script>
